WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.850
A car speeds up, so its speed-time graph curves upward.

00:00:03.850 --> 00:00:06.440
How far does it go in four seconds?

00:00:06.440 --> 00:00:10.420
Distance is speed times time: the area under the graph.

00:00:10.420 --> 00:00:13.870
Four rectangles give about ten point five metres.

00:00:13.870 --> 00:00:17.080
Eight thinner ones: about thirteen point one.

00:00:17.080 --> 00:00:20.070
Thirty-two: about fifteen point three.

00:00:20.070 --> 00:00:24.540
Thinner and thinner, the total closes in on exactly sixteen metres.

00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:27.200
That limit is the area under the curve.

